<title>SINGAPORE: Mobil says refinery operations unaffected by fire.</title>
<headline>Mobil says refinery operations unaffected by fire.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mobil Oil Singapore said on Wednesday its 300,000 barrels-per-day refinery suffered a fire on Monday, but that operations were not affected.</p>
<p>&quot;The incident of May 27 was a minor fire which was put out within half an hour. There were no injuries or impact on refinery operations,&quot; Mobil said in a statement.</p>
<p>The fire, caused by a gas leak, is the fifth accident at the refinery this year. A gas leak in March at its petrochemical complex led to two deaths.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65-8703082)</p>
</text>
